# Evey configuration.
#
# This file holds only what must exist BEFORE the server boots: secrets,
# container wiring (ports, paths, image tag) and reverse-proxy facts.
#
# Everything an operator tunes afterwards - log level, language, transcoding
# limits, hardware acceleration, library watcher, plugin sandbox & quotas -
# lives in the admin panel (Admin → Server config), NOT here. Those settings
# are stored in the database, survive a container recreate, and most apply
# without a restart. Setting them as env vars only seeds a first boot.

# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
MEDIA_DIR=/path/to/your/media

# ── Secrets (only when you bring your own Postgres or Meilisearch) ───────────
# The image embeds both and generates their secrets on first boot, stored in
# ./evey-data/keys (postgres.password, meili.key) - nothing to set for the
# default install. Set these ONLY when the database or the search engine runs
# outside the evey container; an explicit value always wins over the file.
# The repository's own docker-compose.yml runs Postgres as a sibling service
# (EVEY_DB_HOST=postgres), so it needs EVEY_DB_PASSWORD.
EVEY_DB_PASSWORD=changeme
# MEILI_MASTER_KEY=<run: openssl rand -hex 16>

# ── Server ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public URL: used for e-mail links, OIDC redirects and cast/device URLs.
EVEY_SERVER_BASE_URL=http://localhost:9091
EVEY_HTTP_PORT=9091
# EVEY_SERVER_NAME=Evey
# EVEY_VERSION=latest

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Embedded by default: Postgres runs inside the evey container when
# EVEY_DB_HOST is unset (data in ./evey-data/postgres). Set EVEY_DB_HOST to use
# an external one; EVEY_EMBEDDED_POSTGRES=true|false overrides the detection.
EVEY_DB_USER=evey
EVEY_DB_NAME=evey
# 'disable' is correct for the bundled Postgres on a private Docker network
# (the default 'prefer' negotiates TLS pointlessly and logs a warning).
EVEY_DB_SSLMODE=disable

# ── Metadata & intro providers - FIRST-BOOT SEED ONLY ────────────────────────
# These keys are read once, copied into the database, and from then on the
# admin panel is the source of truth (Admin → Server config → API keys).
# You can delete them from this file after the first successful boot.
# TheIntroDB is optional: a Bearer key raises 100 → 500 lookups/day.
# TMDB works out of the box: the image ships a built-in read token (migration
# 000154). Set yours here or in the panel to replace it - yours always wins.
EVEY_TMDB_API_KEY=
EVEY_OMDB_API_KEY=
EVEY_INTRO_TIDB_API_KEY=

# ── Reverse proxy ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EVEY_DOMAIN feeds every bundled proxy example (Caddy, Nginx, Traefik).
# Set the other two whenever a proxy terminates TLS in front of Evey, or
# client IPs (rate limiting, logs) and generated links will be wrong.
# See docs/reverse-proxy.md - it also lists the CSP tokens a curating proxy
# must keep ('wasm-unsafe-eval', gstatic) for browser AC-3 and Chromecast.
# EVEY_DOMAIN=media.example.com
# EVEY_FORWARDED_PROTO=true
#
# EVEY_TRUSTED_PROXIES: which peers may set the client's real IP via
# X-Forwarded-For. Evey checks the IMMEDIATE TCP peer (unforgeable) against
# this list; only then does it read the header. Loopback (127.0.0.1/32, ::1/128)
# is ALWAYS trusted and cannot be removed - the server's own HTTP->gRPC gateway
# uses it - so whatever you set here is ADDED to it, never a replacement.
# Entries may be CIDRs or bare addresses; a malformed one stops the boot.
#
# 172.16.0.0/12 is the Docker private range - the value to use when your proxy
# runs as a container next to Evey (it covers every Docker bridge network, so
# it keeps working when the network is recreated with a different subnet).
#
# It is deliberately broad, so scope it as tightly as your setup allows:
#   * prefer the ONE subnet your proxy actually sits on (`docker network
#     inspect <net>` → e.g. 172.18.0.0/16), not the whole /12;
#   * anything that can open a TCP connection to Evey from inside that range
#     can claim any client IP - which mainly means defeating per-IP login
#     rate limiting and poisoning audit/login history. That requires code
#     execution on the host or in a co-located container.
#   * the strongest hardening is not a narrower CIDR: it is to stop publishing
#     Evey's port on the host at all (drop the `ports:` mapping of the `evey`
#     service) so the proxy is the only thing that can reach it.
# EVEY_TRUSTED_PROXIES=172.16.0.0/12

# ── Hardware transcoding (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# GID of the host's `render` group, for /dev/dri GPU passthrough (VAAPI).
# Find it with: getent group render
# Leave unset to use the default (104); a wrong value = no GPU access and
# Evey silently falls back to software transcode. Enable the acceleration
# itself from the admin panel, not here.
# EVEY_RENDER_GID=104

# ── Email (optional - enables password recovery + notifications) ─────────────
# EVEY_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# EVEY_SMTP_PORT=587
# EVEY_SMTP_USERNAME=
# EVEY_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# EVEY_SMTP_FROM=noreply@example.com
# EVEY_SMTP_TLS=starttls

# ── SSO / OIDC (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EVEY_OIDC_ENABLED=false
# EVEY_OIDC_ISSUER=
# EVEY_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# EVEY_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=
# EVEY_OIDC_ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=

# ── Backups (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EVEY_BACKUP_INTERVAL_HOURS=0
# EVEY_BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=30
